              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "UserInput : {{$context.$system.$inputMessage}}\nHistoryRecords: {{$context.$nodes.FINDHISTORY.$output.items}}\nUserRequestDate : f user has mentioned a date in UserInput then Extract user request date from UserInput otherwise save {{$context.$system.$currentDate}} as UserRequestDate.\n\n\n** If HistoryRecords length == 1, then return result as \"NoHistoryAvailable\", else return result as \"HistoryAvailable\".\n\n** Identify EffectiveStartDate matching UserRequestDate:\n      -- From HistoryRecords the EffectiveStartDate of a history row having EffectiveStartDate of the history row less than or equal to UserRequestDate and EffectiveEndDate greater than or equal to the UserRequestDate is the history row matching UserRequestDate and save the EffectiveStartDate of the row as EffectiveStartDateOfCurrentVersion and EffectiveEndDate of the row as EffectiveEndDateOfCurrentVersion.\n\n** If EffectiveStartDateOfCurrentVersion and EffectiveEndDateOfCurrentVersion is extracted, then return result as \"HistoryAvailable\", else return result as \"NoHistoryAvailable\".\n\n** If HistoryRecords length > 0,  EffectiveStartDateOfCurrentVersion and EffectiveEndDateOfCurrentVersion is extracted then:\n\n1. If from UserInput, the user wants to view earlier version then:\n     Rule: From HistoryRecords identify the history row having EffectiveEndDate just less than 1 day from EffectiveStartDateOfCurrentVersion.\n     1.a. If no such row exists as per rule given in HistoryRecords then return EffectiveStartDate as null.\n     1.b. If such row exists as per rule given in HistoryRecords then return the identified row's EffectiveStartDate as VersionEffectiveStartDate.\n\n2. If from UserInput, the user wants to view later version then:\n     Rule: From HistoryRecords identify the history row having EffectiveStartDate just 1 day greater from EffectiveEndDateOfCurrentVersion.\n     2.a. If no such row exists as per rule given in HistoryRecords then return EffectiveStartDate as null.\n     2.b. If such row exists as per rule given in HistoryRecords then return the identified row's EffectiveStartDate as VersionEffectiveStartDate."
            }
          ],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n    \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n    \"type\": \"object\",\n    \"properties\": {\n        \"VersionEffectiveStartDate\": {\n            \"type\": \"date\"\n        },\n        \"result\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n        }\n    }\n}",
          "type": "LLM",
          "diagram": {
            "x": 5225,
            "y": 7426
          }
        },
