          "code": "SHOWPOSITION",
          "id": "1768984514675",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1768984514676_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "Your goal is to show below mentioned table sections:\n\n## A. Conditional History Section:\n\nIf {{$context.$nodes.FINDHISTORY.$output.items}} is not empty then Show History details as a table:\n* Section header as History:\n * Show section headers, above the table with Bold text.\n* History: {{$context.$nodes.FINDHISTORY.$output.items}}.\n* Always show in HTML table with columns as Effective Start Date, Effective End Date, Changed Attributes, DEHLastUpdateDate as Last Update Date, DEHLastUpdatedBy as Last Updated by.\n* Show Row number column without any column header. \n* DEHLastUpdateDate value should be trimmed to date of  format.\n\nIf {{$context.$nodes.FINDHISTORY.$output.items}} is empty then, DO NOT show {{$context.$nodes.FINDHISTORY.$output.items}}.\n\n## B. Mandatory Table Sections:\n\n1. Create a table having 2 columns:\n * Section header will be Position Details:\n * Show section headers, above the table with Bold text.\n * First column will have attribute name(40% width), second column will have data(60% width).\n * Position Details : {{$context.$nodes.FINDPOSITION.$output.items}} \n         Only show fields EffectiveStartDate, EffectiveEndDate, Status, PositionName, PositionCode, ParentPositionName, BusinessUnitName, DepartmentName, JobName, LocationName, RegularTemporary, FullPartTime, HiringStatus, PositionType. HeadCount, FTE, BudgetAmount, GradeLadder, EntryGradeName.\n\n2. Create a table having 3 columns:\n * Section header will be Valid Grades:\n * Show section headers, above the table with Bold text.\n * First column will have attribute Serial No.(20%width), second column will have Attribute.(40%width) and third column will have Data.(40%width).\n * Valid Grades : {{$context.$nodes.FINDPOSITION.$output.items}} \n         Here, in Serial No. column just show Row No. and in Attribute show field Grade Name, Grade Code, Grade Set in multiple lines under same row and respective values in Data. Show multiple records in multiple rows with row no. as attribute.\n * Branching rule to add(Not to be displayed)\n  - If 0 results:  show “No valid grades found.”  text, and terminate ,do not show an empty table for zero results.\n        \n3. Create a table with multiple columns:\n  * Header will be Incumbents:\n  * Show section headers, above the table with Bold text.\n  *Incumbents : {{$context.$nodes.GETPOSITIONINCUMBENTS.$output.items}}\n   Only show fields Person Number(20% width), Person Name(20% width), Assignment Name(20% width), Status(20% width), Assignment Type(20% width).\n  * Branching rule to add(Not to be displayed)\n  - If 0 Incumbents:  show “No incumbents found.” text ,do not show an empty table for zero results.\n  - If >0 Incumbents: show top 10 Incumbents by latest PositionEntryDate as HTML table and terminate.\n  - If >10 Incumbents, Include message:  \"Total Incumbents present :\" No. of items present in result.\n\n4. Create a table with multiple columns:\n  * Header will be Open Requisitions : \n  * Show section headers, above the table with Bold text.\n  * Requisitions : {{$context.$nodes.GETPOSITIONREQUISITION.$output.items}}\n  * Only show records which have CurrentStateName in [\"Canceled\", \"Expired\", \"Filled\", \"Not Posted\", \"Posted\", \"Scheduled\", \"Suspended\", Unposted\", \"In Progress\"].\n  Only show fields Requisition Number(30% width), Title(40% width) and Current State Name(30% width) in same order\n  * Branching rule to add(Not to be displayed)\n  - If 0 results: show “No open requisitions found.” text ,do not show an empty table for zero results.\n  - If >=1 result: show the HTML table and terminate\n\n\nMANDATORY:\n- Always render results strictly inside valid HTML table tags (<table>...</table>) with proper HTML structure.\n- Add at least one line space before and after every HTML table.\n- Style the table header row with background: medium grey.\n- Ensure all tables have visible borders around every cell and use border-collapse: collapse.\n- Strictly follow these rules and present data with proper column widths, borders, and the defined styling.\n- Provide clear spacing between sections (e.g., margin-top or padding) to separate multiple tables or content blocks."
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM",
          "diagram": {
            "x": 5900,
            "y": 9310
          }
        },
