          "code": "FINDSUMMARYDATES",
          "id": "1768986298731",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1768986298733_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "UserInput : {{$context.$system.$inputMessage}}  \nHistoryRecords: {{$context.$nodes.FINDHISTORY.$output.items}}  \n\nif user has mentioned a single date in UserInput:  \n    --UserRequestDateStart : Extract user request date from UserInput otherwise save {{$context.$system.$currentDate}} as UserRequestDateStart.  \n    --UserRequestDateEnd : Save {{$context.$system.$currentDate}} as UserRequestDateEnd.  \n\nif user has not mentioned any date in UserInput:  \n      eg: User: \"Show me the modification done on position Admin between current version and previous version.\"  \n          or User: \"Show me the modification done on position Admin between current version and next version.\"  \n\n1. Find 'R_current' in HistoryRecords where  \n   EffectiveStartDate <= {{$context.$system.$currentDate}} AND EffectiveEndDate >= {{$context.$system.$currentDate}}  \n\n2. Set (based on intent):  \n   a) if user asks \"current version and previous version\":  \n      --UserRequestDateEnd = {{$context.$system.$currentDate}}  \n      --UserRequestDateStart = R_current.EffectiveStartDate - 1 day  \n\n   b) if user asks \"current version and next version\":  \n      --UserRequestDateStart = {{$context.$system.$currentDate}}  \n      --UserRequestDateEnd = (R_current.EffectiveEndDate + 1 day)  \n\nIf user wants to view modified attributes between date range in system, then  \n     eg: User: \"Show me the modification done between 01-January 2020 to 01-January 2025 of position Admin.\"  \n    --UserRequestDateStart: Extract Starting date for this date range and store as UserRequestDateStart.  \n    --UserRequestDateEnd: Extract ending date for this date range and store as UserRequestDateEnd.  \n\n** Identify RangeStart and RangeEnd based on UserRequestDate**:  \n      Rule: From HistoryRecords select records falling on or after the extracted UserRequestDateStart and on or before the extracted UserRequestDateEnd. Skip history record having FirstDESplitFlag true.  \n      --Extract EffectiveStartDate value from each selected HistoryRecords as per Rule and store as String in an Array.  \n      --Return the Array as selectedEffectiveStartDates.  \n\n**Example Response**:  \n->return selectedEffectiveStartDates = [\"2024-01-01\",\"2025-01-01\",\"2025-10-01\"]"
            }
          ],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n    \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n    \"type\": \"object\",\n    \"properties\": {\n        \"selectedEffectiveStartDates\": {\n            \"type\": \"array\",\n            \"items\": {\n                \"type\": \"string\"\n            }\n        }\n    }\n}",
          "type": "LLM",
          "diagram": {
            "x": 6800,
            "y": 7204
          }
        },
