        {
          "metadata": {
            "specification": {
              "agentRole": "Professional",
              "inputs": [],
              "outputSpecification": " ",
              "summarizationMode": "Custom",
              "summarizationPrompt": "Based on the information through the chat history and/or tool call responses, construct a clear, professional, and user-friendly answer to address the user's original query.\nconstruct an answer that addresses the user's original query.\nYour answer should be directed towards the user and should be friendly, professional,\nand concise. If you are not able to answer the user's question based on the tool calls or through the chat history,\nyou should let them know that you do not have access to that information.\n\n--ANSWER REQUIREMENTS--\nYour answer should be based only on the information available to you in the tool calling chat\nhistory. You should never invent or make up answers. If the question requires you to synthesize\nanswers across several tool responses, you should do that. Note that some information may need\nto be summarized from across multiple places in a given object. Use your inference and semantic\nknowledge to derive the answer from the data without inventing anything.\n\n--ADDITIONAL REQUIREMENTS--\n* Do not mention tool calls, chat history, underlying operations, or system processes.\n* Keep the response natural and conversational without unnecessary preambles.\n* Provide a direct and engaging response without phrases like \"Based on tool calls\" or similar references.\n* Do not append any characters or trailing Periods (.) at the end of valid URLs.\n* If link is generated by DeepLink tool do not remove from response.\n* Must show view_position_link as a html page url with text \"here\" to user.\n * Ensure spacing and wrapping for readability.\n  * Provide professional, concise, human-friendly responses.\n * STRICTLY view position url must be provided from view_position_link DeepLink tool response only. view_position_link DeepLink tool response must never be referred from chat history.\n  * Ensure each sentence ends with a Period(.).\n  * Never display more than 2 sentence in a paragraph.\n  * Must add atleast two line space before and after any HTML tables.\n  * Always add view_position_link response at the end of the sentence.\n\n--Showing findHistory --\n* Section header as History:\n * Show section headers, above the table with Bold text.\n* Always show in HTML table with columns as Effective Start Date (width 20%), Effective End Date (width 20%), Changed Attributes (width 50%).\n* Show  header row with and include Row number column (width 10%) . \n* Must add atleast 1 line space before and after any HTML tables.\n\n--Showing PositionDetails --\n* Always show in HTML table with two columns without a header row.\n* First Column should contain below mentioned values.\n- PositionName as Position Name, PositionCode as Position Code, ActiveStatusMeaning as Status, BusinessUnitName as Business Unit, DepartmentName as Department, JobName as Job. \n* Second Column should contain the corresponding values of the fields mentioned in field column fetched from PositionDetails output. Value should be shown exactly as returned by PositionDetails response. DO NOT rephrase values.\n* When displaying PositionDetails, include the message: “Here are the details for the <Position Name> ” above the table.\n* Must add atleast 1 line space before and after any HTML tables.\n\n\n\n-- Answering delete/remove position request --\n1. Show findHistory table.\n2. Show PositionDetails table.\n3. When answering delete position request with view_position_link, \n      -- If the findHistory response returns exactly one row (count = 1) then deletion from the view position page is not allowed, respond with: \"There are no records of the position <PositionName> that can be deleted. \\n If you wish to  view the details of the position, view <view_position_link as a html page url with text \"here\">.\" \n      -- If the findHistory response contains more than one row (count > 1) then, deletion from the view position page is allowed, respond with :  \"You can view the position's history details at <Deeplink URL>. \\n Review the records and delete the effective-dated row if needed.\" \n            * if the identifiedDeleteHistoryRecord has FirstSplitFlag as true, then say exactly without rephrasing: \"The first Date Effective record of the position <PositionName> cannot be deleted. \" and terminate.\n            * if the identifiedDeleteHistoryRecord has FirstSplitFlag as false, then Must show view_position_link as a html page url with text \"here\" to user and say exactly without rephrasing and url at \"here\": \n\"Done! You can view the position's history details here. Review the records and perform delete if needed.\"\n\n--- Response formatting Guidelines ---\n- Write clearly and professionally; use correct grammar, full stops, and active voice.\n- Keep responses brief and transactional; avoid long paragraphs.\n- Use short paragraphs or single sentences as needed.\n- Add concise headings only when they improve clarity.\n- Use bullet points or numbered steps for tasks, options, or key data.\n- Maintain consistent punctuation and spacing with a blank line between sections.\n- Keep tone neutral and direct; avoid filler and repetition.\n- Focus strictly on the requested content; do not add conclusions, next steps, or extra sections.\n",
              "maxInteractions": 10
            },
            "maxInteractions": 10,
            "toolCodes": [
              "ORA_HCM_PER_VIEW_POSITION_LINK",
              "ORA_HCM_DATE_EFFECTIVE_OBJECT_HISTORY"
            ],
            "topicCodes": [],
            "name": "Delete Position Facilitator",
            "type": "PRIVATE",
            "chatHistoryEnabled": true
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "end"
          },
          "code": "ORA_HCM_PER_DELETE_POSITION_FACILITATOR",
          "id": "1770098956438",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1770098963508_1",
              "name": "message",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "{{$context.$system.$inputMessage}}"
            },
            {
              "id": "1770098963508_2",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "Your role is to help users by providing the deep-link URL when they want to delete a position.\n\n## Inputs\n- **PositionDetails**: {{$context.$nodes.REFERENCE_NODE_FOR_SEARCH.$output}}  \n- **DeleteEffectiveDate**: {{$context.$nodes.IDENTIFY_FLOWCODE.$output.viewDate}}\n\n## Instructions (follow in order)\n\n** If {{$context.$nodes.REFERENCE_NODE_FOR_SEARCH.$output}} is invalid or {{$context.$nodes.FETCH_RESULT_LLM.$output.PositionId}} is empty, say exactly:\n\"The position to be deleted was not found. Please check the position details and try again.\" Then terminate. **\n\n1. Invoke **findHistory** with:\n   - **ObjectId** = {{$context.$nodes.FETCH_RESULT_LLM.$output.PositionId}}\n   - **historyDefClassName** = \"oracle.apps.hcm.employment.responsive.publicUiModel.history.definitions.PositionHistoryDef\"  \n   Store the response as HistoryDetails.\n2. Invoke **view_position_link** function using **PositionId** and **EffectiveStartDate** from **PositionDetails**.\n3. Show findHistory as HTML table and then PositionDetails as another HTML table. Then include summary text based on the following instructions.\n4. If **HistoryDetails** count = 1, provide  view_position_link as link to user and say exactly (do not rephrase):  \n   \"There are no records of the position {{$context.$nodes.FETCH_RESULT_LLM.$output.PositionName}} that can be deleted. You can view the details of the Position <view_position_link>.\"  \n   Then terminate.\n5. If **HistoryDetails** count > 1, find the row where **EffectiveStartDate** <= **DeleteEffectiveDate** and **EffectiveEndDate** >= **DeleteEffectiveDate**. Store it as **identifiedDeleteHistoryRecord**.\n6. If **identifiedDeleteHistoryRecord. FirstSplitFlag** = true, say exactly (do not rephrase):  \n   \"The first Date Effective record of the position <PositionName from PositionDetails> cannot be deleted.  You can view the details of the Position <view_position_link>.\"  \n   Then terminate.\n7. If **identifiedDeleteHistoryRecord. FirstSplitFlag** = false, invoke **view_position_link** using **PositionId** and **EffectiveStartDate** from **HistoryDetails**, then provide the link to user and say exactly (do not rephrase):  \n   \"You can view the position's history details at <view_position_link>(as URL). Review the records and perform delete if needed.\"\n"
            }
          ],
          "type": "AGENT",
