          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1770043789136_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "Your task is to show search position results to user. \n\nParse the following JSON string into an object named `searchData`:\n\n{{$context.$nodes.REFERENCE_NODE_FOR_SEARCH.$output}}\n\nYour task is to show search position results to user.\n\nsearch_results : Check the search results from searchData.searchResults.searchResponse.response.items.\n\n--If the output contains valid search results, assign them to `search_results` and display them as an HTML table. \n--If the output is empty, invalid, or contains an error, respond with \"No matching positions found.\"\n\nUserInput : {{$context.$system.$inputMessage}} \nFilterBy : Extract filterBy attribute from UserInput.\n\n-The user can narrow down the position search by specifying filter criteria for the following attributes in scope:\n  --HasValidGrade \n  --GradeName \n  --GradeCode \n  --PositionReports \n  --EffectiveDate \n  --IncumbentName \n  --IncumbentPersonNumber\n  --HasIncumbent\n  --Status\n  --StatusCode \n  --Type \n  --TypeCode \n  --HiringStatus\n  --HiringStatusCode\n  --BusinessUnitId \n  --BusinessUnit \n  --AncestorPositionName \n  --AncestorPositionCode \n  --ParentPositionId \n  --ParentPositionName \n  --ParentPositionCode \n  --DepartmentTitleId \n  --DepartmentTitle \n  --DepartmentNameId \n  --DepartmentName \n  --LocationId \n  --LocationName \n  --LocationCode\n  --JobId \n  --JobName\n  --JobCode\n  --PositionName \n  --PositionCode \n\n-If the user mentions a blank filter attribute in {{$context.$system.$inputMessage}}, it is a out of scope request.\n\n--Showing search_results---\n\n* MANDATORY: Always display results as a single HTML table only—never in an array, object, JSON, or other data structure.\n* HTML Table header row background: medium grey;\n* Include these columns in this order: Name, Code, Status, Business Unit Name, Department Name.\n* Set column widths: Name 15%, Code 15%, Status 10%, Business Unit Name 15%, Parent Position 16%, Department 16%, Job 13 % . * Style the table with visible borders and border-collapse: collapse; style the header row with a grey background. \n* Do not use bullet lists, plain text lines, or any other format.\n* Branching rule to add\n- If 0 search_results: show “No matching positions found.”\n* if 0 search_results then analyse {{$context.$system.$inputMessage}} and if user has tried to query for any attribute out of scope attribute, then include the following message. \"The search criteria used is not supported.\".  Ensure proper line spacing between sentences.\n* if 0 search_results then analyse {{$context.$system.$inputMessage}} and if user has not tried to query for any attribute out of scope and has used a valid filter attribute, then do not show any additional message.\n* Do not include or end with a follow up question or user action. Do not mention/list the supported filter criteria to user.\n- If >=1 result: show the HTML table (only top 10 results) \n* When showing HTML table, display this message above the table (replace <keyword> with the search term): \"Here are the top search results for <keyword> search.\" If UserInput  has filter by mentioned, then include phrase, \"filtered by <FilterBy>\".\n* Always show only first 10 records. Do not mention the count. Show message inviting user action (e.g., \"To view a position, please select a position code.\")\n* Do not include any items array, object, or implementation details—convert data into the table format for display only.\n* Do not provide style or implementation explanations to the user.\nWhen providing search results, your response must be only a rendered HTML table (preceded by the instructional message), never an array, object, or JSON.\n\n\n--Explicit requirements:\n\n* In {{$context.$system.$inputMessage}} if user has mentioned to search for blank or null attributes, then must show politely declining message that you cannot perform a blank search on attributes.\n\n*Return your output as plain HTML/text only, to be directly shown to the user.\n  DO NOT mention or output any JSON syntax, arrays, objects, or key-value pairs.\n  DO NOT escape HTML as a string or include markup in quotes.\n  Show a maximum of 10 records, and do not show an empty table for zero results.\n  To summarize: Your entire output should be exactly what the user will see—just the instructional message,   the fully-rendered HTML table, and the action prompt if appropriate. \n  There should be no additional   wrapping, meta-data, or structure of any kind.\n\n\n* Example HTML content:\nPositionId                    Name\t                               Code\t                  Status\t Parent Position      Business Unit\t              Department                           Job\n------                             ------                                    ------                          ------      ----------------      -----------------------     ----------------------         -----------\n300100676535544   Division Manager\tDivision_Manager\tActive       Sales Director\t    Division Sales Head\tGlobal High Tech Sales   Manager\n\n* To view a position, ask user to reply with the position code to view."
            },
            {
              "id": "1779086593115_systemPrompt",
              "name": "systemPrompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "Read input from : {{$context.$nodes.REFERENCE_NODE_FOR_SEARCH.$output.searchResults}}"
            }
          ]
        },
