        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "specification": {
              "agentRole": "Professional",
              "inputs": [],
              "outputSpecification": "",
              "summarizationMode": "Custom",
              "summarizationPrompt": "Based on the information through the chat history and/or tool call responses, construct a clear, professional, and user-friendly answer to address the user's original query.\nconstruct an answer that addresses the user's original query.\nYour answer should be directed towards the user and should be friendly, professional,\nand concise. If you are not able to answer the user's question based on the tool calls or through the chat history,\nyou should let them know that you do not have access to that information.\n\n--ANSWER REQUIREMENTS--\nYour answer should be based only on the information available to you in the tool calling chat\nhistory. You should never invent or make up answers. If the question requires you to synthesize\nanswers across several tool responses, you should do that. Note that some information may need\nto be summarized from across multiple places in a given object. Use your inference and semantic\nknowledge to derive the answer from the data without inventing anything.\n\n--ADDITIONAL REQUIREMENTS--\n* Do not mention tool calls, chat history, underlying operations, or system processes.\n* Keep the response natural and conversational without unnecessary preambles.\n* Provide a direct and engaging response without phrases like \"Based on tool calls\" or similar references.\n* Do not append any characters or trailing Periods (.) at the end of valid URLs.\n* Do not remove any Periods (.) at the end of valid sentences.\n* If link is generated by DeepLink tool do not remove from response.\n* Must show the Create a Requisition link as a HTML page url with link text as \"here\".\n* Must show the Request a Position Change link as a HTML page url with link text as \"here\".\n* When showing create_requisition_for_a_position link, in a separate paragraph say exactly: \n\"You can click here to create a requisition for the position.\" and must include create_requisition_for_a_position output as a html page url at text \"here\".\n* When showing request_a_position_change link, in a separate paragraph say exactly: \n\"You can click here to request a position change for the position.\" and must include request_a_position_change output as a html page url at text \"here\".\n\n--- Response formatting Guidelines ---\n- Write clearly and professionally; use correct grammar, full stops, and active voice.\n- Keep responses brief and transactional; avoid long paragraphs.\n- Use short paragraphs or single sentences as needed.\n- Add concise headings only when they improve clarity.\n- Use bullet points or numbered steps for tasks, options, or key data.\n- Maintain consistent punctuation and spacing with a blank line between sections.\n- Keep tone neutral and direct; avoid filler and repetition.\n- Focus strictly on the requested content; do not add conclusions, next steps, or extra sections.",
              "maxInteractions": 10
            },
            "maxInteractions": 10,
            "toolCodes": [
              "ORA_HCM_PER_CREATE_REQUISITION_FOR_A_POSITION_LINK",
              "ORA_HCM_PER_REQUEST_A_POSITION_CHANGE_LINK"
            ],
            "topicCodes": [],
            "name": "Create Position Facilitator",
            "type": "PRIVATE",
            "chatHistoryEnabled": true
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "end"
          },
          "code": "ORA_HCM_PER_CREATE_POSITION_FACILITATOR",
          "id": "1768989307746",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1768989327667_1",
              "name": "message",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "{{$context.$nodes.ASKUSERPICKPOSITION.$feedbackRecieved}}"
            },
            {
              "id": "1768989327667_2",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "**Purpose\nGiven a user’s request and a REST response of position details, determine the intended flow, extract required identifiers, construct the correct deep links, and present only the relevant links to the user.\n\n**Inputs\n- UserInput:  {{$context.$system.$inputMessage}}\n- RestResponse: {{$context.$nodes.SHOWVACANTCHILDPOSITIONS.$output.result.PastIncumbentDetails}}\n- effectiveDate: {{$context.$system.$currentDate}}\n\n##Step 1: Derive flowname and Position from UserInput\n- If the user asks to “create requisition” for a position:\n  - flowname = CreateRequisition\n  - Position = the named position\n- If the user asks to “request a position change” for a position:\n  - flowname = RequestPositionChange\n  - Position = the named position\n- If the user mentions only a position (e.g., “Position Developer”) or explicitly asks for both:\n  - flowname = RequestPositionChangeAndCreateRequisition\n  - Position = the named position\n\nExamples:\n- “Create requisition for position Developer.”\n  - flowname: CreateRequisition, Position: Developer\n- “Request a position change for position Developer.”\n  - flowname: RequestPositionChange, Position: Developer\n- “Position Developer.”\n  - flowname: RequestPositionChangeAndCreateRequisition, Position: Developer\n- “Request a position change and create requisition for position Developer.”\n  - flowname: RequestPositionChangeAndCreateRequisition, Position: Developer\n\n##Step 2: Extract identifiers from RestResponse\nFrom RestResponse, find the record matching Position and extract:\n- PositionId\n- BusinessUnitId\n- EffectiveStartDate (use the position’s effective start date; if multiple entries exist, select the one relevant to effectiveDate or the most recent effective start date not after effectiveDate)\n\n##Step 3: Construct appropriate deep link URLs\nUsing PositionId, BusinessUnitId, and EffectiveStartDate, build the deep links required for the flow:\n- Create Requisition deep link\n- Request Position Change deep link\n\nNote: Use your standard HCM deep link patterns for these actions, substituting:\n- {PositionId} with the extracted PositionId\n- {BusinessUnitId} with the extracted BusinessUnitId\n- {EffectiveStartDate} with the extracted or resolved EffectiveStartDate\n\n##Step 4: Present links based on flowname\n- If flowname is CreateRequisition or RequestPositionChangeAndCreateRequisition:\n  - Show the Create a Requisition deep link as a HTML url.\n- If flowname is RequestPositionChange or RequestPositionChangeAndCreateRequisition:\n  - Show the Request a Position Change deep link as a HTML url.\n\nError handling and clarifications\n- If Position cannot be determined from UserInput, prompt the user to specify the position.\n- If no matching Position is found in RestResponse, inform the user and ask them to confirm the position name.\n- If required identifiers are missing, notify the user that the deep link cannot be constructed and request missing data."
            }
          ],
          "type": "AGENT",
          "diagram": {
            "x": 11093,
            "y": 5666
          }
